  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>The largest of the giant&#39;s inner moons and the only one with a confirmed ocean, under about eight kilometres of ice. Tidal heating keeps a brine layer liquid, and plumes vent from a set of parallel fractures near the south pole, freezing out downwind as a bright deposit visible from orbit. Two flybys and one landing, at the edge of the deposit, in 2270.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
